From 6ea8dcd311b194e0d3d5fbf7e70cdb43a45a5c49 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 04:46:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] core, web: hardware-file refusals are one sentence

Why: set_controls, set_buffer_mode, set_frames_per_folder, set_clip_merge
and set_storage_preroll refused through errorReplyBody, with a machine code,
the revision, issue lists and a conflicts array beside the error. The page
branched on the code and added its own "Press Reload" text. Original Apertar
refuses every command with errorReply(id, sentence) and shows that sentence
as written (ApertarCoreApp.cpp:108-128@upstream-1.6.0; CMD-9, CMD-28).

What: the five commands refuse with errorReply(command.id, result.error).
The store's conflict sentence ends "Reload, then change it again.", as the
two stale sentences already do. The page shows Core's sentence on a refused
Hardware, Controls or Undo save and on a refused Check, with no list. Check
sends the loaded revision (no "h" fallback) and is disabled until the page
has one. The store's merge path (textToEdits, conflicts, needs_review,
confirm_merge, the merged member) and the script-path refusal are kept.
A text Check already answers ok with its issues (whole-file saves are not
refused on new errors), so the store needs no dry-run change.

Tested: check_core.sh both builds and 18 host tests pass. --simulate with a
hardware file: a key edit adding an error, a conflict, a stale base on all
five commands and APERTAR_SCRIPT_PATHS=ssh each answer one sentence; a stale
values-only text save still answers merged/needs_review. Chromium against
--simulate: Check disabled before load, Check lists the error, stale and
refused Controls/Hardware saves show Core's sentence and keep the edits.
smoke + shape_subset: every 1.6.0 field present with the same type.
Camera: nothing; no hardware path changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NEFc1w7Y8dcyiV489BiwMr
